 **Delegation**:
-Launching a child with a role and a TaskSpec. Two entry points: `planner_delegate` always mints a new Task (it takes no `taskId`) and returns the canonical `taskId`; `planner_redelegate` binds an existing Task by that verbatim id for a correction round, a review, or a recovery re-execution. Rebinding reads the complete stored TaskSpec and never accepts caller fields that redefine it; optional instructions augment one child packet only, while the invocation role selects routing without changing the stored role. Workspace admission compares the stored workspace to the host context cwd. `planner_tasks` is the read-only lookup that lists this workspace's live Tasks (memory plus ledger records the restore cap left out) when the canonical id is not in context. The child's WorkerReport returns launcher-validated, never parsed from text; at most one worker per cwd. Ordinary worker, explorer, and validator executions use finite default anomaly bounds (`maxTokens=100000`, `maxWallMs=600000`) unless an operator configuration or explicit `envelope` replaces them; the source is persisted. A breach fires CANCEL and records `worker_runaway` on the TaskExecutionRecord. Reviewer invocations remain Request-bounded.
